n: 7.2 g/dL (severe anemia)", "Platelets: 28,000/μL (thrombocytopenia)", "Basophilia: 8%", "LDH: 2,450 U/L (elevated)", "Uric acid: 11.2 mg/dL (elevated)", "Peripheral smear: left-shifted granulocytes at all stages of maturation", "Philadelphia chromosome (Ph) positive", "BCR-ABL1 fusion gene detected (p210 transcript)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute Leukemia without Ph+ translocation: Ph+ chromosomal finding makes this less likely, but remains in differential as blasts are present", "Hodgkin lymphoma: No lymphadenopathy described; Ph+ is atypical for lymphoma, but included as a competing mechanism due to constitutional signs", "Myelodysplastic syndrome: Typically presents with low blasts in bone marrow rather than peripheral blood; included in differential until confirmed"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (night sweats, fatigue)", "Severe pancytophenia (elevated WBC with blasts and severe anemia/thrombocytopenia)", "Massive splenomegaly", "Retinal hemorrhages and cotton-wool spots (suggesting microvascular involvement)", "Petechiae (bleeding diathesis due to low platelets and blasts)", "Philadelphia chromosome positivity (specific indicator of clonal myeloid proliferation)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4240837696335079, "posterior": 0.32015810276679846, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Myeloid lineage commitment in peripheral blood (left shift) definitively excludes lymphoid blast etiologies (B2 and B5) by eliminating lymphopenia/lymphoid immunophenotype as a potential explanatory mechanism.", "Ph+ positivity combined with myeloid lineage commitment (left shift) eliminates lymphoid and non-malignant leukocytosis as explanations for the blast increase."], "evidence_against": ["Ph+ p210 and 3-week subacute presentation with myeloid maturation arrest strongly suggest CML blast crisis rather than de novo AML, as the Ph+ translocation is specific to clonal MPNs with documented progression.", "The combination of Ph+/BCR-ABL1 p210 with a subacute clinical course argues against de novo AML in favor of clonal progression of CML to blast crisis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Presence of Philadelphia chromosome or BCR-ABL1 fusion gene detected", "History of chronic MPN vs. de novo presentation"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy for blast percentage and myeloid lineage evaluation", "Flow cytometry for blast immunophenotype"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.47120418848167545, "posterior": 0.6403162055335969, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["82% blasts with Ph+ BCR-ABL1 p210 transcript fulfill WHO diagnostic criteria for CML blast crisis, making this the best explanatory model in the differential.", "The combination of Ph+/BCR-ABL1 p210 with a subacute clinical course argues against de novo AML in favor of clonal progression of CML to blast crisis."], "evidence_against": ["High blast percentage (82%) and peripheral blood involvement argue against chronic/accelerated CML phases which typically have blasts <20% in peripheral blood, but are consistent with blast crisis as a sub-phase of B3."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of MPN symptoms evolving over months?", "Presence of basophilia or left-shift on smear"], "requestable_discriminators": ["KIT mutation testing", "Peripheral blood flow cytometry for li